  "pr-rule": {
    "file": "pr-rule.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "In a sentence, the stressed and unstressed syllables combine to make rhythm.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "2f1ce14089bf0fbe"
  },
  "prs-1": {
    "file": "prs-1.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "If you cycle, it'll help the Earth.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "a593de767cdb6c3a"
  },
  "prs-2": {
    "file": "prs-2.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "Water is good for your body.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "7881d106ef81c05d"
  },
  "prs-3": {
    "file": "prs-3.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "The students are planting trees in the garden.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "8fa291728d40e44b"
  },
  "prs-4": {
    "file": "prs-4.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "Is it better to use paper bags?",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "7f1f46a863850fc8"
  },
  "prs-5": {
    "file": "prs-5.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "We are happy to walk to school.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "cb915e9986608ffd"
  },
  "prd-01": {
    "file": "prd-01.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "What are you doing?",
    "voice": "en-GB-LibbyNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "e388954cc2af15d1"
  },
  "prd-02": {
    "file": "prd-02.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "I'm writing an article about going green.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "6ff17d636add7710"
  },
  "prd-03": {
    "file": "prd-03.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "Great! I'm writing a poem about the three Rs.",
    "voice": "en-GB-LibbyNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "9a5ff9eeb8f283df"
  },
  "prd-04": {
    "file": "prd-04.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "Let me read it.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "dcef9df015aaa918"
  },
  "prd-05": {
    "file": "prd-05.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "I'm still writing. Wait for a minute.",
    "voice": "en-GB-LibbyNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "07a38b9eeb679443"
  },
  "gr-a1": {
    "file": "gr-a1.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "There are two kinds of articles in English: the indefinite article (a / an) and the definite article (the).",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "58665ef8ee77ba48"
  },
  "gr-a2": {
    "file": "gr-a2.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "We use a / an",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "3cb6ccd1fa811699"
  },
  "gr-a3": {
    "file": "gr-a3.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "with singular countable nouns when we are talking about them in general.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "f5b25bc87c53e3df"
  },
  "gr-a4": {
    "file": "gr-a4.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "An ant is a tiny animal.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "c235cd5a14ce87e8"
  },
  "gr-a5": {
    "file": "gr-a5.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "after the verbs to be and to have.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "eb07bcf45e113e74"
  },
  "gr-a6": {
    "file": "gr-a6.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "I'm a student.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "8ed976bd1dd8c8f8"
  },
  "gr-a7": {
    "file": "gr-a7.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "I have an eraser.",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "29b11f454b827497"
  },
  "gr-a8": {
    "file": "gr-a8.mp3",
    "kieu": "don",
    "text": "We use the",
    "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
    "rate": "+0%",
    "bam": "2d06fb9eee1048cf"
  },
  "gr-a9": {
